---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../../lib/url';
import { INSTITUTION_COUNT, NETWORK_NAME, REVIEW_TIME } from '../../../site.config.mjs';
---

<SiteLayout title="About" current="about">
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-12 md:py-16">
    <p class="eyebrow">About the network</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl sm:text-5xl">Connecting disciplines to advance precision and personalised nutrition</h1>

    <div class="prose-page">
      <p class="text-lg">
        The {NETWORK_NAME} connects researchers across disciplines, students, clinicians and other professionals to
        advance nutrition approaches tailored to individuals and communities.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our goal is to build the capacity, skills and collaborations needed to translate precision and personalised
        nutrition research into practice and improve population health.
      </p>
      <p>
        The network provides a shared place to find datasets, connect with collaborators, exchange resources and develop
        skills. It brings together expertise from nutrition and dietetics, medicine, biomedical science, engineering, data
        science, statistics and other relevant fields, with opportunities to connect research, clinical practice and
        policy.
      </p>

      <h2>Our aims</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Enable data discovery and reuse.</strong> Help members find existing datasets and connect with their custodians, making better use of participants’ contributions and research investment.</li>
        <li><strong>Build multidisciplinary collaborations.</strong> Connect people with complementary expertise to address questions that expand beyond traditional disciplinary boundaries.</li>
        <li><strong>Strengthen capacity and capability.</strong> Share resources, practical knowledge and learning opportunities to help members develop and apply new skills.</li>
        <li><strong>Support emerging researchers.</strong> Create opportunities for students and early-career researchers to connect with mentors, supervisors and collaborators.</li>
        <li><strong>Advance research into practice.</strong> Support collaboration that helps bring precision and personalised nutrition into healthcare and community settings to improve health.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        We are a multidisciplinary network connecting people with a shared interest in advancing precision and
        personalised nutrition. Researchers from {INSTITUTION_COUNT} Australian institutions have joined the network.
      </p>
      <p>
        The network is overseen by a leadership committee of six researchers from organisations across several Australian
        states, including New South Wales, Victoria and Western Australia. The committee guides the network’s activities,
        manages requests and oversees the directory and its review process.
      </p>

      <h2>How listings are reviewed</h2>
      <p>
        Every dataset listing and skills profile is reviewed by a member of the leadership committee before it appears in
        the directory.
      </p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Submit your listing.</strong> It is saved as pending and is not visible to others while it is reviewed.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>We review your submission.</strong> Within {REVIEW_TIME}, a committee member checks the relevant
          information. For dataset listings, this includes confirming that the submission describes the data without
          including research data files or information that could identify participants, that you are the custodian or
          have their permission, and that information about consent for secondary use is provided.
        </li>
        <li><strong>We contact you if needed.</strong> We approve the listing or email you with questions or an explanation if it cannot be listed.</li>
        <li><strong>Your approved listing is published.</strong> It appears in the directory with the dates it was listed and last reviewed.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>We check that listings remain current.</strong> Each year, we ask dataset custodians and profile owners
          to confirm their information is current. Listings may be removed if we don’t hear back within 30 days.
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        You can update or remove your listing at any time. See <a href={withBase('/privacy/')}>Privacy and terms</a> for
        details.
      </p>

      <h2>Data access and responsibilities</h2>
      <p>
        The directory helps people discover datasets and contact their custodians. The network does not hold or host
        research data, or grant permission to access it.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>The person submitting a listing is responsible for ensuring that the information they provide is
        accurate, complete and kept up to date</strong>, and that they have the authority or the custodian’s permission to
        submit it. The network is not responsible for the accuracy or completeness of information supplied by
        contributors.
      </p>
      <p>
        Each custodian decides who may use their data and on what terms, and remains responsible for relevant ethics
        approvals, participant consent and data access agreements. Inclusion in the directory is not an endorsement of a
        dataset or an individual.
      </p>

      <h2>Get involved</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href={withBase('/submit/')}><strong>Submit a dataset listing</strong></a> to help others discover your data and discuss potential collaboration.</li>
        <li><a href={withBase('/submit/profile/')}><strong>Join the skills directory</strong></a> to share your expertise and connect with collaborators.</li>
        <li><a href={withBase('/resources/')}><strong>Become a member</strong></a> to access shared resources and learning opportunities, including recordings, templates and protocols.</li>
        <li><a href={withBase('/contact/')}><strong>Contact the leadership committee</strong></a> with questions, suggestions or ideas for the network.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>
